<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="015" project="spaarke-dataset-grid-framework-r2">
  <metadata>
    <title>FR-04: Wizard placement checks + runtime dev-guard for `widthPreference`</title>
    <phase>2: Wizard UI + Per-Instance Overrides</phase>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <estimated-hours>2</estimated-hours>
    <dependencies>013,014</dependencies>
    <blocks>016</blocks>
    <tags>frontend, typescript, react, fluent-ui, workspace-layout-wizard, wizard-ui, dev-guard</tags>
    <rigor-hint>FULL</rigor-hint>
    <rigor-reason>Modifies `.tsx` + `.ts` files; wizard UI logic + runtime dev-guard; interacts with FR-04 metadata (task 014)</rigor-reason>
    <parallel-group>Wave 7</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Same file (`WorkspaceLayoutWizard/src/App.tsx`) touched by 011, 013 — must serialize; also modifies `sectionRegistry.ts`</parallel-reason>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>
    Add wizard placement UI logic: when a `widthPreference: 'full'` widget is dropped into a multi-slot row, prompt a modal "This widget needs full width — convert row to single-column?" (Yes / Cancel). When a `widthPreference: 'half'` widget is placed in a single-slot row, show a subtle warning icon + hover tooltip. Add runtime dev-guard in `sectionRegistry.ts` that logs `console.warn` when a `'full'` widget renders in a multi-column row.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    SPAARKE frontend wizard-UX contributor + framework dev-guard implementer.
  </role>

  <goal>
    Wizard blocks/warns on invalid placements per widthPreference. Runtime dev-guard fires `console.warn` on violations. Both use section metadata from task 014.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      FR-04's schema half (task 014) added the field. This task exposes it: wizard prompts on invalid placements; runtime warns on violations that slipped through.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>src/solutions/WorkspaceLayoutWizard/src/App.tsx</file>
      <file>src/solutions/LegalWorkspace/src/sectionRegistry.ts</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-021">Fluent v9 modal + tooltip conventions.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Modal offers Yes / Cancel; NOT a hard block — operator can force by editing JSON directly.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Runtime dev-guard uses `console.warn` (not `console.error`) — dev signal, not user-facing error.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Runtime dev-guard only fires in DEV mode (`process.env.NODE_ENV !== 'production'`).</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>projects/spaarke-dataset-grid-framework-r2/CLAUDE.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarke-dataset-grid-framework-r2/spec.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-021-fluent-design-system.md</file>
      <file>.claude/patterns/ui/fluent-v9-component-authoring.md</file>
    </files>
  </knowledge>

  <steps>
    <step order="1">Read spec.md § FR-04. Read `WorkspaceLayoutWizard/src/App.tsx` (placement handler) and `sectionRegistry.ts` (existing drift check ~lines 141-179).</step>
    <step order="2">In wizard: when user drops a section into a row slot, check `sectionMetadata.widthPreference` for that section. If `'full'` and row has multiple columns (> 1 slot), open a Fluent v9 `Dialog` with title "Full-width widget", body "This widget renders best at full row width. Convert this row to a single column?", buttons "Yes, convert" (default) / "Cancel (keep row)".</step>
    <step order="3">In wizard: when a `'half'` widget lands in a single-slot row, show a Fluent v9 `Tooltip` on hover of the section chip: "This widget is designed for half-width rows; a single-column row may leave excess whitespace."</step>
    <step order="4">In `sectionRegistry.ts`: add a runtime check (existing drift check ~lines 141-179 or nearby). For each rendered section, if `metadata.widthPreference === 'full'` and the section is in a multi-column row, `console.warn('[Spaarke DataGrid] Section {sectionId} has widthPreference:full but is rendered in a multi-column row. Consider moving to a single-column row.')`. Guard with `NODE_ENV !== 'production'`.</step>
    <step order="5">Unit test on runtime dev-guard: mock a section with `widthPreference: 'full'` in a multi-column context → `console.warn` called; same section in single-column context → no warn; `NODE_ENV === 'production'` → no warn regardless.</step>
    <step order="6">Wizard integration test: dropping a `'full'` widget in a `1fr 1fr` row triggers the modal; clicking "Yes" converts the row; clicking "Cancel" leaves it.</step>
    <step order="7">`npm test` + `npm run build` — clean.</step>
    <step order="8">Update TASK-INDEX.md: → ✅.</step>
  </steps>

  <tools>
    <tool name="npm">Build + test</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/solutions/WorkspaceLayoutWizard/src/App.tsx (modified — placement modal + tooltip)</output>
    <output type="code">src/solutions/LegalWorkspace/src/sectionRegistry.ts (modified — runtime dev-guard)</output>
    <output type="test">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/WorkspaceShell/__tests__/widthPreferenceGuard.test.ts (new)</output>
    <output type="test">src/solutions/WorkspaceLayoutWizard/src/__tests__/widthPreferencePlacement.test.tsx (new)</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Wizard opens modal when `'full'` widget dropped into multi-slot row; buttons Yes/Cancel work.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Wizard shows tooltip on `'half'` widget in single-slot row.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Runtime dev-guard: `console.warn` fires when `'full'` widget in multi-column row + NODE_ENV != production.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Runtime dev-guard silent in production (`NODE_ENV === 'production'`).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Unit + integration tests + build clean.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>
    - `sectionRegistry.ts` lives at `src/solutions/LegalWorkspace/src/sectionRegistry.ts` (not under `WorkspaceShell/`). This file may relocate to the new shared package as part of FR-10 (task 021) — plan for the relocation but don't do it here.
    - Task 015 is the last piece of Phase 2. Task 016 closes with deploy + PR 2.
    - If Fluent v9 `Dialog` is heavy for a simple confirm, consider `MessageBar` with action buttons — either is acceptable per ADR-021.
  </notes>

  <execution>
    <skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill>
    <protocol>Load knowledge. FULL rigor. Step 9.5 quality gates. UI test defs below.</protocol>
  </execution>

  <ui-tests>
    <test name="Full-width modal on multi-column drop">
      <steps>
        <step>Open WorkspaceLayoutWizard</step>
        <step>Create row with `1fr 1fr` columns</step>
        <step>Drag Communications section into that row</step>
        <step>Verify modal appears with "Convert to single column?"</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>Modal prompts; both buttons functional</expected>
    </test>
    <test name="Runtime warning in dev mode">
      <steps>
        <step>Deploy layout with Communications in a `1fr 1fr` row (edit JSON directly to bypass wizard)</step>
        <step>Open LegalWorkspace in browser with DevTools console</step>
        <step>Check for warning: "widthPreference:full but rendered in multi-column row"</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>console.warn appears in dev mode; silent in prod build</expected>
    </test>
    <test name="Dark mode compliance (ADR-021)">
      <steps>
        <step>Toggle dark mode</step>
        <step>Trigger the placement modal</step>
        <step>Verify modal + tooltip render correctly</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>Fluent v9 semantic tokens throughout</expected>
    </test>
  </ui-tests>
</task>
